The resulting dataset becomes the single source of business intelligence for all downstream forecasting activities.

---

# Benefits

## Standardized Features

Every forecasting model consumes identical business intelligence.

---

## Model Independence

Business intelligence is separated from forecasting implementation.

New forecasting models require no changes to feature engineering logic.

---

## Reproducibility

Demand Intelligence datasets can be regenerated from certified Gold datasets.

---

## Reusability

The same intelligence supports:

- forecasting
- capacity planning
- simulations
- reporting
- AI assistants

---

## Explainability

Business intelligence remains understandable to operational stakeholders because features are generated through standardized enterprise logic.

---

## Scalability

Additional intelligence modules can be introduced without affecting forecasting models.

---

# Consequences

## Positive

- reusable forecasting intelligence
- standardized feature engineering
- simplified model experimentation
- improved explainability
- cleaner architecture
- easier maintenance
- future AI readiness

---

## Trade-offs

- additional processing layer
- additional storage
- additional metadata management

These trade-offs are acceptable because they significantly improve architectural consistency and forecasting reliability.

---

# Alternatives Considered

## Feature Engineering Inside Each Model

Rejected.

Reasons:

- duplicated logic
- inconsistent features
- difficult maintenance
- unreliable comparisons between models

---

## Direct Forecasting from Gold Layer

Rejected.

Reasons:

- Gold datasets are analytical, not predictive
- feature engineering becomes fragmented
- reduced explainability
- poor scalability

---

## Notebook-Specific Feature Engineering

Rejected.

Reasons:

- inconsistent implementations
- difficult governance
- duplicated business logic
- poor reusability

---

# Rationale

Demand Intelligence represents the transition between Enterprise Data Engineering and Enterprise AI Engineering.

Separating business intelligence from forecasting creates a clean architectural boundary where:

- enterprise data engineering produces trusted information
- enterprise AI consumes standardized predictive intelligence

This enables:

- fair model comparison
- reusable forecasting pipelines
- explainable AI
- future Feature Store integration
- future real-time forecasting
- enterprise decision intelligence

---

# Decision Outcome

The AI Workforce Capacity Planning Platform formally adopts an independent Enterprise Demand Intelligence Architecture.

Demand Intelligence becomes a permanent enterprise layer responsible for producing standardized business intelligence before any forecasting model is executed.

All future forecasting models, simulations, optimization engines, and AI services must consume Enterprise Demand Intelligence outputs rather than performing independent feature engineering.

